$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a stirring solution of crude
arylthiazol-2-yl-amine (0.42 mmol) in acetic acid was added bromine in
acetic acid (0.42 mmol). The reaction was further stirred for 1 h at room
temperature after which the solvent was removed in vacuum. The resulting
residue was purified by HPLC (C18 column, eluted with CH3CN/H2O with
0.035% TFA) to give (5-bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-aryl-amine as a solid. Yields
varied from 20% to 90%. (5-Bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-pyridin-4-yl-amine (62)
Compound 62 was synthesized using the same method as described for
(5-bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-pyridin-2-yl-amine (60). 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 7.66
(s, 1H), 7.94 (d, 2H, J = 5.6 Hz), 8.59 (d, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz), 12.16 (bs,
1H); m/z [M++1] 255.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Selective Aminothiazole Aurora Kinase Inhibitors
