$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Halogenated 3-Thienyloxyacetic Acids (7):;
General Procedure: N-Bromo- or N-chlorosuccinimide (0.025 mol or 0.05
mol) for the monohalogenation or dihalogenation, respectively, is added
to a solution of the respective 3-thienyloxyacetic (6; 0.025 mol) in
chloroform/acetic acid (1/1; 30 ml). The reaction is monitored by T.L.C.
on silica gel. Chloroform is evaporated from the mixture without heating
in vacuo. Water (50 ml) is added to the residue and the insoluble solid
filtered off and crystallized. Educt: 6b, Product: Halogenated
3-Thienyloxyacetic Acids (7ba). Yield: 88%. m.p.: 93-94°C (heptane or
benzene/heptane), Molecular Formula: C6H4Cl2O3S (227.1), microanalyses
calculated value: C ± 0.29; H ± 0.24; S ± 0.30. 1H-N.M.R.
(solvent/TMSint) δ [ppm]: (DMSO-d6): 7.68 (s) (5-H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reactions with 3-hydroxy-2-(methoxycarbonyl)thiophene; I. Synthesis of
3-thienyloxyacetic acid and its (nuclear) chloro and bromo derivatives
