$DATUM 3-Chlorooctacetyldiosmin (12). Chlorination of 7 (1.42 g, 1.5 mmol) to
compound 12 was performed under the same conditions as previously
described for bromination to 8, by using NCS instead of NBS.
Chlorination, slower than bromination (80 instead of 20 h), afforded 12
as a yellowish, amorphous powder (1.29 g, 88% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
[aglycone moiety] 2.33 and 2.44 (6H, 2s, OAc-5 and 3'), 3.91 (3H, s,
OMe-4'), 6.69 (1H, d, J = 2 Hz, H-6), 6.89 (1H, d, J = 2 Hz, H-8), 7.08
(1H, d, J = 8.8 Hz, H-5'), 7.58 (1H, d, J = 2.2 Hz, H-2'), 7.77 (1H, dd,
J = 8.8 and 2.2 Hz, H-6'); [sugar moiety: inner glucose (") and terminal
rhamnose ('")] 1.13 (3H, d, J= 6.4 Hz, H-6"), 1.92-2.06 (18H, 6s, 6 sugar
acetyls), 3.66 (1H, H-6"), 3.80 (2H, H-6"and H-5"'), 3.94 (1H, H-5"),
4.67 (1H, s, H-1"'), 4.99 (1H, H-4"'), 5.13-5.28 (5H, H-2", 3", 4", 2"',
and 3'''), 5.27 (1H, H-1").
