$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The mixture of 2 (250 mg, 0.45 mmol), LiCl (23 mg, 0.54 mmol), and CAN
(651 mg, 1.19 mmol) in MeCN-AcOH (1:1, 20 mL) was stirred at 80°C for 8
hours. The proceeding of the reaction was followed by TLC (solvent A).
The solvent was evaporated and the residue was partitioned between DCM
(50 mL) and water (2 × 20 mL). The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (40 g silica gel, DCM → DCM-MeOH 9:1). 3a (230 mg) as a
white powder. Yield: 87%. m.p. 136-138°C; R f (A) 0.48; MS (ESI) m/z
[M+H]+ calcd 591.1; found 591.3.
