$DATUM Step 3 To a suspension of methyl iodide (0.73 mL, 11.7 mmol) and sodium
hydride (280 mg, 7.00 mmol) in DMF (30 mL) at 0 °C was added
2-fluoro-3-(4-iodo-1H-pyrazol-1-yl)propan-1-ol (Enantiomer A from step 2)
(630 mg, 2.33 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient
temperature for 1 h, then diluted in EtOAc (300 mL) and washed with H2O
(50 mL). The organic layer was separated and dried over MgSO4. The
solution was filtered and concentrated in vacuo, then purified by flash
column chromatography (0-100% EtOAc/Hexanes gradient) to give 575 mg of
1-(2-fluoro-3-methoxypropyl)-4-iodo-1H-pyrazole (87%). 1H NMR (600 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 7.91 (s, 1H); 7.55 (s, 1H); 5.01-4.88 (m, 1H); 4.42-4.33 (m,
2H); 3.60-3.52 (m, 1H); 3.50-3.42 (m, 1H); 3.28 (s, 3H). LRMS (ESI)
calc’d for (C7H11FIN2O) [M+ H]+, 285.0; found 284.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
