$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (b) Experimental procedure for formation of undesired product
(5'chloro-2'-furoyl) 5-ethoxycarbonyl-Δ2-isoxazoline by NCS and DMAP in
organic media 2-Furoylaldoxime (1e, 102 mg, 1.07 mmol) was dissolved in
dry dichloromethane (3 mL) in a 10 mL round bottom flask and kept at -5
oC under nitrogen atmosphere. N-Chlorosuccinimide (190 mg, 1.42 mmol) and
molecular sieve (~0.2 gm) were added into it and stirred for 1 hr. A
mixture of 4-dimethylaminopyridine (145 mg, 1.19 mmol) and ethyl acrylate
(150 mg, 1.5 mmol) in dichloromethane (2 mL) was added to the reaction
mixture and stirred for 1 h. It was allowed to attain room temperature.
The reaction was complete in 3 days. The reaction mixture was filtered
through sintered funnel and the organic layer was washed with cold
aqueous HCl (0.5N, 2x20 mL) and cold water (3x20 mL), dried on anhydrous
sodium sulphate and concentrated in a rotary evaporator under reduced
pressure at room temperature. The crude product was chromatographed over
silica-gel (5% EtOAc in petroleum ether). Isolated yield was 85% (221 mg,
0.9 mmol). (5'chloro-2'-furoyl) 5-ethoxycarbonyl-Δ2-isoxazoline(3i),
yield 85% (221 mg, 0.9 mmol). Compounds 3i is known in the literature and
thus spectroscopic data, elemental analysis data and NMR spectra were not
given.5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
