$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4,5-Dichloro-7-[2-deoxy-3,5-bis-O-(2-methylpropanoyl)-β
-Derythro-pentofuranosyl]-2-(formylamino)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine
(8a); Typical Procedure To a solution of compound 7 (1.1 g, 2.43 mmol) in
DMF (30 mL) was added N-chlorosuccinimide (390 mg, 2.92 mmol). After
stirring for 24 h at 50 °C, the reaction mixture was evaporated to
dryness, redissolved in CH2Cl2 and chromatographed (silica gel, column 4
× 12 cm, A → B). From the main zone, a colorless foam was obtained.
Crystallization from CH2Cl2-petroleum ether (2:1).
5-Bromo-4-chloro-7-[2-deoxy-3,5-bis-O-(2-methylpropanoyl)-β
-D-erythro-pentofuranosyl]-2-(formylamino)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3- d]pyrimidine
(8b) As described for 8a, the reaction was carried out with 7 (1.1 g,
2.43 mmol) and N-bromosuccinimide (516 mg, 2.90 mmol, 5 h) in DMF or
CH2Cl2 (30 mL). FC resulted in a colorless foam of 8b. Crystallization
from CH2Cl2-petroleum ether (2:1) yielded colorless crystals (1.08 g,
84%). Mp 121 °C; TLC (silica gel, B): Rf = 0.42. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6): δ =
1.06 (d, 6 H, J= 6.9 Hz, 2 CH3), 1.13 (d, 6 H, J= 6.9 Hz, 2 CH3),
2.53-2.67 (m, 3 H, 2 CH, H-2'), 2.87-2.99 (m, 1 H, H-2'), 4.19-4.27 (m, 3
H, H-4', 2 H-5'), 5.34-5.37 (m, 1 H, H-3'), 6.53 (t, 1 H, J= 6.8 Hz,
H-1'), 7.98 (s, 1 H, H-6), 9.38 (d, 1 H, J = 9.5 Hz, NH), 11.21 (d, 1 H,
J= 9.5 Hz, HCO). UV (MeOH): λmax (ε) = 250 nm (39400). Anal. Calcd for
C20H24BrClN4O6 (531.8): C, 45.17; H, 4.55; N, 10.54. Found: C, 45.57; H,
4.62; N, 10.33.
